  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: 7 Bridge. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Seven Bridge (7 Bridge) is a Japanese Rummy game. 2-5 players. 52-card deck. 7 cards each. Special rule: 7s need only 2-card melds (e.g., 7-7 or 6-7 is valid). Single 7 can be played as 1-card meld. Draw from stock (discard pile restricted). Lay off on any meld. Go out by melding all but last card + discard. All-at-once meld = double score.',
    objective: 'Form melds (sets or sequences), lay off on existing melds, and be the first to go out by melding or laying off all cards except one and discarding that final card.',
    gameplay: "Draw from stock (discard pile only if immediately melding). Meld sets (3-4 same rank) or runs (3+ sequential same suit). 7s special: only need 2 cards for meld (7-7 valid set, 6-7 valid run). Single 7 = 1-card meld. Lay off on any player's melds. Discard to end turn. All-at-once go-out = double score.",
